      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0267",
    "text": "A spherical Earth helps explain why observers in different places see different stars and shadows. It joins local observations into one model.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2568,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-spherical-earth",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0268",
    "text": "A spherical Earth",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2569,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-spherical-earth",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0269",
    "text": "Different stars and shadows at different places support a curved Earth. Adding the measured distance between observing places makes it possible to investigate the size of that whole Earth.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2570,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-measurable-earth",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0270",
    "text": "An Earth whose size can be investigated",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2571,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-measurable-earth",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0271",
    "text": "Records collected over generations let astronomers compare planetary movements. Greek astronomy also drew on earlier Babylonian observations.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2572,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-planetary-archive",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0272",
    "text": "An archive of planetary motion",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2573,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-planetary-archive",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0273",
    "text": "Ptolemy's Earth-centered model predicts celestial positions using combined circular motions. Its historical value includes what it could predict, not just what later accounts changed.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2574,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-ptolemaic-model",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0274",
    "text": "Ptolemy\u2019s predictive heavens",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2575,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-ptolemaic-model",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0275",
    "text": "A model of planetary motion may accurately predict where a planet appears. That success does not, by itself, establish every physical cause or assumption in the model.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2576,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-model-not-cause",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0276",
    "text": "A forecast is not its physical cause",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2577,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-model-not-cause",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0277",
    "text": "Gears can represent repeating movements in the sky. A physical model makes those cycles visible without explaining every cause of them.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2578,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-mechanical-sky",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0278",
    "text": "A sky represented in gears",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2579,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-mechanical-sky",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0279",
    "text": "Different versions of a text are kept visible for comparison. Their differences become evidence about how the work was copied and changed.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2580,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-textual-variants",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0280",
    "text": "A text with visible alternatives",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2581,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-textual-variants",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0281",
    "text": "Translators carry logical arguments into Arabic while developing terms for their distinctions. The texts become available for new teaching and debate.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2582,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-arabic-logic",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0282",
    "text": "Logic in a new scholarly language",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2583,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-arabic-logic",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0283",
    "text": "Arabic-speaking scholars use, criticize and develop inherited accounts of nature. Translation supports new inquiry rather than simply storing old knowledge.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2584,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-arabic-nature",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0284",
    "text": "Natural philosophy in Arabic",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2585,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-arabic-nature",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0285",
    "text": "Arabic-speaking astronomers use new observations to criticize difficulties in Ptolemy's inherited sky model. Learning from an older work can lead to revision rather than unquestioning acceptance.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2586,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-ptolemy-questioned",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0286",
    "text": "Ptolemy read critically",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2587,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-ptolemy-questioned",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0287",
    "text": "Place-value notation gives a practical way to record and work with quantities. This mathematical tradition did not come from a single Greek source.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2588,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-positional-reckoning",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0288",
    "text": "Place-value reckoning",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2589,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-positional-reckoning",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0289",
    "text": "Relations between known and unknown quantities can be studied before the unknown value is found. This makes a problem easier to state and reason about.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2590,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-algebraic-relations",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0290",
    "text": "Reasoning about an unknown share",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2591,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-algebraic-relations",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0291",
    "text": "Avicenna distinguishes what a thing is from whether it exists. A thing that could exist or fail to exist still needs an explanation for why it exists at all.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2592,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-contingent-being",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0292",
    "text": "Avicenna: contingent existence",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2593,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-contingent-being",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0293",
    "text": "Avicenna argues that things whose existence depends on something else require a source that does not depend on another. His proposed necessary being answers why dependent things exist at all.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2594,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-necessary-being",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0294",
    "text": "Avicenna: a necessary source of existence",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2595,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-necessary-being",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0295",
    "text": "A commentary becomes new inquiry when it tests and develops the older argument. Receiving a tradition can also change it.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2596,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-active-commentary",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0296",
    "text": "A commentary that changes the question",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2597,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-active-commentary",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0297",
    "text": "Some theories say sight works through rays leaving the eye, while another account studies light entering it. Comparing the claims turns familiar seeing into a question that observations can test.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2598,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-vision-dispute",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0298",
    "text": "Rival accounts of sight",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2599,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-vision-dispute",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0299",
    "text": "Ibn al-Haytham explains sight through light entering the eye. This directs inquiry toward light sources, paths and viewing conditions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2600,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-light-into-eye",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0300",
    "text": "Sight depends on light entering the eye",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2601,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-light-into-eye",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0301",
    "text": "Drawing light paths helps explain images and sight. Geometry connects the arrangement of objects with where their light arrives.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2602,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-geometric-optics",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0302",
    "text": "Light paths as a geometric account",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2603,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-geometric-optics",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0303",
    "text": "Light passing through the small opening forms an upside-down image on the screen. The dark box makes the faint image easier to see.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2604,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-inverted-image",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0304",
    "text": "An inverted image on the screen",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2605,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-inverted-image",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0305",
    "text": "The glass has been shaped into a convex lens. Held at a suitable distance, it can make a nearby object appear larger.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2606,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-ground-lens",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0306",
    "text": "A convex magnifying lens",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2607,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-ground-lens",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0307",
    "text": "The lens bends light so that a nearby object appears larger. The view depends on how the lens and object are positioned.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2608,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-magnified-view",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0308",
    "text": "A magnified close-up view",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2609,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-magnified-view",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0309",
    "text": "Light entering the eye does not explain every judgment we make about what we see. Distance, size and other features can still be misread.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2610,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-seeing-and-judging",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0310",
    "text": "Seeing includes interpretation",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2611,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-seeing-and-judging",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0311",
    "text": "Latin translations make Aristotle's works available in new schools and debates. Readers also encounter different interpretations of those works.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2612,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-latin-aristotle",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0312",
    "text": "Aristotle in Latin",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2613,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-latin-aristotle",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0313",
    "text": "Commentators disagree about what an older argument means and whether it succeeds. There is no single uncontested reading.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2614,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-commentaries-in-dispute",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0314",
    "text": "The commentators disagree",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2615,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-commentaries-in-dispute",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0315",
    "text": "Aquinas distinguishes truths investigated by natural reason from truths accepted through revelation. The distinction does not make the two inquiries identical.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2616,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-reason-faith-distinction",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0316",
    "text": "Reason and faith: distinct questions",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2617,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-reason-faith-distinction",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0317",
    "text": "An objection receives a reasoned reply in an organized debate. The format makes disagreement explicit; it does not guarantee agreement.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2618,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-formal-disputation",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0318",
    "text": "An objection and an accountable reply",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2619,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-formal-disputation",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0319",
    "text": "A realist account says that separate things share a real common nature. Medieval versions differ from Plato's theory of separately existing Forms.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2620,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-real-universal",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0320",
    "text": "A shared nature beyond this instance",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2621,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-real-universal",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0321",
    "text": "A nominalist account uses common names and concepts for separate things without positing a shared universal thing outside the mind. This is more than rejecting Plato's separate Forms.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2622,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-nominal-kinds",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0322",
    "text": "Common concepts, not a shared thing outside the mind",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2623,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-nominal-kinds",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0323",
    "text": "A realist account says separate things share a real common nature. A nominalist account groups individuals through names and concepts without such a shared thing outside the mind. Placing them together identifies the disagreement, not a final compromise.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2624,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-universals-open",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0324",
    "text": "One shared name, rival accounts",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2625,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-universals-open",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0325",
    "text": "Do not add things to an explanation when they do no work. A shorter explanation is not automatically true; it must still account for the evidence.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2626,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-explanatory-economy",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0326",
    "text": "Do not multiply idle explanations",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2627,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-explanatory-economy",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
