        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-ancient-wisdom-claim",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0341",
    "text": "Renaissance readers had treated the writings attributed to Hermes as extremely ancient. Evidence from their language places them later. This weakens the appeal to antiquity without automatically refuting every idea they contain.",
